{"id": "4ff0d05e-e8e6-4d13-911f-922f0cd2d94a", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This is a bounded question — checking the lifecycle policy against what happened to `v3.1.0`, plus a risk scan of other tags — so let me dig into it directly rather than open a full investigation.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_CUUgFSRfaOIrFq6BmQmaOq", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether the ECR lifecycle policy on the 'checkout-service' repository caused the image tag 'v3.1.0' to be deleted yesterday, and identify what other tags/images in that repo are at risk of deletion under the current lifecycle policy.",
  "context": "User reports tag v3.1.0 disappeared from ECR repo checkout-service yesterday, and an ECS service failed to start as a result (likely because it referenced that tag/digest). Need to confirm root cause (lifecycle policy expiry vs manual deletion vs something else) and assess risk to other images -- especially any still referenced by running ECS task definitions, Lambda functions, or other consumers.",
  "resources": ["ECR repository: checkout-service", "ECS services/task definitions referencing checkout-service images"],
  "timeframe": "last 48 hours (to cover 'yesterday' relative to 2026-10-30T20:51:54Z), plus current lifecycle policy state",
  "criteria": [
    "Fetch the current ECR lifecycle policy for checkout-service and evaluate its rules against image push dates/counts to see if v3.1.0 would have matched an expiration rule",
    "Check CloudTrail for ECR delete/lifecycle execution events around the time v3.1.0 disappeared to confirm whether lifecycle policy, manual DeleteImage call, or lifecycle execution triggered the removal",
    "List current images/tags in checkout-service and determine which ones would be deleted under the existing lifecycle policy on its next evaluation",
    "Cross-check any at-risk tags against what's actually in use (ECS task definitions currently referencing the repo, Lambda functions using container images from it) to flag any that would break something if deleted",
    "Report back: confirmed cause of v3.1.0 deletion, list of at-risk images/tags, and which of those are currently in use by ECS/Lambda"
  ]
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze ECR checkout-service lifecycle policy and recent image deletions"}], "created_at": null}
